   3+ 8000              ; Diagnostic policy: normal builds suppress per-IN/OUT trace. Set to 1
   4+ 8000              ; temporarily when investigating a specific guest port sequence.
   5+ 8000              P126_DEBUG_IO_TRACE EQU 0
   6+ 8000              ; Guest I/O devices are software models on NeoGS. No guest port number is
   7+ 8000              ; ever issued as a physical NeoGS/Z80 I/O operation.
   8+ 8000              ;
   9+ 8000              ; Implemented:
  10+ 8000              ;   0000h-000Fh, 0080h-0083h: 8237 address/count, controller and page registers.
  11+ 8000              ;   0020h-0021h: 8259A master PIC register model and CPU acknowledge path.
  12+ 8000              ;   0040h-0043h: 8253 channel programming, latches and static readback.
  13+ 8000              ;   0060h-0063h: PCem-compatible XT keyboard/PPI port handler.
  14+ 8000              ;   00E0h: retained 16-bit diagnostic test latch.
  15+ 8000              ;   Keyboard FIFO is idle after reset; XT BAT response AAh is queued only
  16+ 8000              ;   when PB6 has a low-to-high edge. ATM keyboard input remains a future IPC
  17+ 8000              ;   producer; no physical NeoGS I/O is involved.
  18+ 8000              ;   DMA transfer engine and PIT clock/IRQ0 are separate services.
  19+ 8000              ;
  20+ 8000              ; PCem keyboard_xt.c owns the observable 60h-63h handler:
  21+ 8000              ;   60h = keyboard data latch/FIFO, 61h = XT system-control PB,
  22+ 8000              ;   62h = board configuration/speaker status, 63h = open bus (FFh).
  23+ 8000              ; PCem ppi_reset() initializes PA=00h/PB=40h, while keyboard_xt.pb itself
  24+ 8000              ; starts at 00h. The XT handler reads its own PB latch, so this model keeps
  25+ 8000              ; the keyboard PB latch at 00h until the guest writes port 61h.
  26+ 8000
